    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d749">

                <pb facs="0857" n="845" sameAs="frus:frus1943v02/pg845"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00112 European War 1939/8631: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in the United
                        Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-06-09">June 9, 1943</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3596. Your 3714, May 21 and 3838, June 5. In view of your statement in 3714, May
                    31, Department and BEW agree that substance of communication to be delivered to
                    the Swiss may take the form stated in your 3838, June 5.</p>
                <p>We will be prepared to take parallel action here on June 10.<anchor n="31"
                        xml:id="d749-f1"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d749-f1" n="31" xml:id="d749-f1-content">
                <p>Text of the memorandum presented to the Swiss Legation on June 10 was
                    substantially the same, <hi rendition="#italic">mutatis mutandis</hi>, as that
                    quoted in telegram No. 3838, <hi rendition="#italic">supra</hi>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
